/-!
# Fidelity checks for the second entry (`ChallengeKN.lean`) — NOT part of any build target

Run with `lake env lean KNChecks.lean` (about 2 min; all `decide +kernel`, no `native_decide`, no `#eval`).
Generated by the scratch scripts `genchecks.py` / tightness generator (see the statement-review notes (research repository)).

1. **Builder witnesses ↦ `IsKN`.** For 9 witness nets of `witnesses/{kn2,kn}` (research repository) (raw generator
   matrices `C_*` exactly as saved by the Python builders `kn2_build1b.py` / `x2_build2.py`), the graph form
   `G_* = C_* B⁻¹` (computed in Python) satisfies `G_* c * B_* = C_* c` (kernel-checked; so `G_*` and `C_*` have
   the same point set) and `IsKN r p k rows_r_p G_*` with the rows of `table1` / `table2`.
2. **Stage-B nets ↦ `IsKNskel`.** Four nets built by the independent Python construction
   the stage-B construction script (research repository) (frame `x2_lib.mobius` + the eliminations of the research notes) satisfy
   `IsKNskel r p k (skB_r ρ)`.
3. **Tightness.** For all 37 designs, `T_p` is attained by a configuration of the relaxation, i.e. `T_p` is the
   exact relaxation minimum (it equals `lb2 · p²` of the C++ certificate `kn2_cert.cpp`).
Negative controls (wrong rows / wrong `ρ`) were run and fail.
-/


namespace Z3NetKN.Checks
open Z3NetKN

/-- Decidable reformulation of `IsKN` (bounded quantifiers in decidable order). -/
theorem isKN_of {r p k : ℕ} {R : Rows} {C : Fin 3 → Matrix (Fin (3 * k + r)) (Fin (3 * k + r)) (ZMod p)}
    (h1 : ∀ c : Fin 3, ∀ j < depth r k c, ∀ col < 3 * k + r,
      ent (C c) j col = if col = off r k c + j then 1 else 0)
    (h2 : ∀ c d : Fin 3, r ≤ (c : ℕ) → ∀ l < depth r k d,
      ent (C c) (depth r k c) (off r k d + l) = ((winEntry (R.sk c d) (win r d) (depth r k d) l : ℤ) : ZMod p))
    (h3 : ∀ c d : Fin 3, ∀ l < depth r k d,
      ent (C c) (jrow r k c) (off r k d + l) = ((winEntry (R.jt c d) (win r d) (depth r k d) l : ℤ) : ZMod p))
    (h4 : ∀ c : Fin 3, ∀ i < 3 * k + r, jrow r k c < i → ∀ l < depth r k c, ent (C c) i (off r k c + l) = 0) :
    IsKN r p k R C :=
  ⟨⟨fun c j col hj hcol => h1 c j hj col hcol, h2⟩, h3, fun c i l hi him hl => h4 c i him hi l hl⟩

